{
  "reason": "Tier 2: replace sampled-softmax with BPR-max ranking loss as one controlled objective change. Sampled-softmax with either eight or 64 negatives remained below the historical binary-loss result of 0.5737, while attention, relative bias, and the identity residual failed to exceed it. This pattern motivates testing whether emphasizing negatives that currently outrank the positive improves ranking, rather than adding more representation components; the trajectory does not establish the underlying cause.",
  "module": [
    "model_design",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": null,
    "model_design": "Replace the current sampled-softmax objective with BPR-max, a Tier 2 loss-component change distinct from the previously tested binary logistic and cross-entropy objectives. For each valid position, compute w = softmax(negative_logits.float(), dim=1), then minimize -log(sum_j w_j * sigmoid(positive_logit - negative_logit_j)) plus 0.001 * sum_j w_j * negative_logit_j.square(), averaged across positions. Implement the ranking term stably as -torch.logsumexp(log_softmax(negative_logits.float(), dim=1) + logsigmoid(positive_logits.float().unsqueeze(1) - negative_logits.float()), dim=1); do not detach the weights. This tests whether concentrating gradients on competitive sampled negatives helps where increasing uniform negative count did not. Preserve GRURec, its constructor, encode, score, predict, all existing architecture attributes including relative_bias and residual_gate, and the jointly trained single-network scoring function.",
    "training_evaluation": "In train_category, replace only the cross-entropy loss calculation, retaining positive_logits, negative_logits, NEGATIVES=64, target-collision resampling, history windows, optimizer, learning rate, AMP, clipping, batch settings, and SASREC_EPOCHS default 200. Preserve train_category(name, device, deadline), write_predict_script(), checkpoint metadata, and predictor routing, with exactly one newly trained selected checkpoint per category and identical validation/inference preprocessing. Retain supplied preprocessing-seed-0 splits, training seed 42, DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], all four categories, trial-local artifacts, and single-GPU execution; do not access hidden tests or create a test submission during search. Keep fixed validation candidates, evaluation seed 42, 200 users per category, 99 unique negatives, and HR@10 checkpoint selection with existing NDCG tie-breaking unchanged, using pinned-host macro HR@10 to compare against the current 0.5637 and historical 0.5737. Verify finite loss and gradients within the same training run, charge execution against the remaining shared budget, and print the measured local macro result with print(f'Final Validation Score: {score}')."
  }
